        "created_at": "2026-02-26T19:38:17.546Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\n\n**What**: Web UI pages lose their filter state when the browser refreshes. For example, filtering tasks by status=in_progress or triage by tag=cli is lost on reload. Filter state should be persisted in URL query parameters so that refreshing preserves the view, and URLs are shareable/bookmarkable.\n\n**Where**: The tasks page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/tasks/+page.svelte`) already partially implements URL-based filters — it reads from `$page.url.searchParams` (line 39-47) via the `filterParams` derived value. However, the triage page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) uses local `$state` variables (`filterTag`, `filterStatus` at lines 43-44) that are NOT synced to URL params. Other list pages (items, inbox) likely have the same issue.\n\nKey files to update:\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte` — filterTag and filterStatus need URL param sync\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/items/+page.svelte` — check if filters use URL params\n- Any other list/filter pages under `packages/web-ui/src/routes/`\n\n**How**: Follow the pattern already established in the tasks page:\n1. Read initial filter values from `$page.url.searchParams` (from `$app/stores`)\n2. When a filter changes, use `goto()` (from `$app/navigation`) to update URL params without a full page reload: `goto(\\`?status=\\${filterStatus}&tag=\\${filterTag}\\`, { replaceState: true, keepFocus: true })`\n3. Use `$derived` to compute filter values from URL params (like tasks page does)\n4. This approach gives: URL persistence, back/forward navigation, shareable links\n\nFor the triage pag
```
